#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: rozum-ucc-chat
version: 2.1.0
description: rozum UCC — chat app that drives a coding agent on the local model. Compiled to chat.html.
---
# rozum — chat (agent + model)

A phone-first CHAT app that drives a coding agent (claude/codex/opencode) on the LOCAL model over a
project. Each message runs the agent HEADLESS and non-interactively — `claude -p "<message>"` etc. via
`/control/coder/launch` — the reliable path the matrix scores 18/18 with (v1's interactive-tmux-REPL
wedged: Claude Code treats a send-keys Enter as a newline, so messages piled up unsent — the "echo
camera" bug; headless has no REPL/PTY to wedge).

v2.1 improvements:
- CLEAN bubbles — strips rozum-launch / claude-banner / sandbox / warning noise; shows the answer.
- MEMORY — threads a compact history of the last turns into the prompt so the agent keeps context
  (prompts stay lean — a heavy system prompt degrades a 4B, see the codex-lean lesson).
- STATUS phases — "loading model…" while the shared gateway warms, "thinking…" while the agent runs.
- PERSISTENCE — the conversation survives a reload (localStorage).

Backend contract (same-origin, control-serve :8411, Face-ID-gated):
- `POST /control/coder/launch  {agent, model, workdir, prompt, verify:false}` → `{id, …}`
- `GET  /control/coder/log?id=&tail=` → `{id, alive, log}`
- `GET  /control/status` → `{installed:[{spec}], projects:[{name,path}], …}`

Compiled via: ssc run chat.ssc → chat.html  (see deploy-ucc-web.sh)

## Page
```scalascript
